 with, and addresses match by exact string comparison — ",[225,243,244],{},"OrderService"," and ",[225,247,244],{}," are two different addresses. Service names carry the case of the class that published them, so a typical address looks like:",[218,250,253],{"className":251,"code":252,"language":223},[221],"srv:\u002F\u002Fos-api~org.kinotic.os.api.services.ProjectService\u002FfindByRepoFullName\n",[225,254,252],{"__ignoreMap":227},[206,256,258],{"id":257},"components","Components",[260,261,263],"h3",{"id":262},"scheme","Scheme",[210,265,266],{},"Identifies the type of resource being addressed.",[268,269,270,282],"table",{},[271,272,273],"thead",{},[274,275,276,279],"tr",{},[277,278,263],"th",{},[277,280,281],{},"Description",[283,284,285,296],"tbody",{},[274,286,287,293],{},[288,289,290],"td",{},[225,291,292],{},"srv",[288,294,295],{},"Published services and their methods",[274,297,298,303],{},[288,299,300],{},[225,301,302],{},"stream",[288,304,305],{},"Event streams (not yet routable through the gateway)",[260,307,309],{"id":308},"scope","Scope",[210,311,312,313,316],{},"An optional qualifier that narrows the CRI to a specific context, such as a tenant ID, user ID, or device ID. When present, it appears before the ",[225,314,315],{},"@"," symbol.",[210,318,319,320,323],{},"If a scope needs sub-scopes, use the format ",[225,321,322],{},"scope:sub-scope",".",[218,325,328],{"className":326,"code":327,"language":223},[221],"srv:\u002F\u002Ftenant-123@app.acme-org.orders-app~OrderService\nstream:\u002F\u002Fdevice-42@app.acme-org.orders-app~temperature\u002Fsensor-1\n",[225,329,327],{"__ignoreMap":227},[260,331,333],{"id":332},"zone","Zone",[210,335,336,337,340],{},"The optional zone places the resource in the isolation boundary the gateway validates on every send and subscribe. It precedes the resourceName, separated by ",[225,338,339],{},"~",". A zone is one or more dot-separated labels of lowercase letters, digits, and interior dashes.",[268,342,343,351],{},[271,344,345],{},[274,346,347,349],{},[277,348,333],{},[277,350,281],{},[283,352,353,366,376,386],{},[274,354,355,360],{},[288,356,357],{},[225,358,359],{},"app.\u003CorganizationId>.\u003CapplicationId>",[288,361,362,363,323],{},"One application's services. Only that application (and system participants) can call them; they are hosted by the owning organization's runtime, which authenticates as an organization participant. Applications may nest their own sub-zones, e.g. ",[225,364,365],{},"app.acme-org.orders-app.billing",[274,367,368,373],{},[288,369,370],{},[225,371,372],{},"app-api",[288,374,375],{},"The platform's data plane for applications, such as entity persistence and named query execution. Hosted in-process by the platform only.",[274,377,378,383],{},[288,379,380],{},[225,381,382],{},"os-api",[288,384,385],{},"The platform services organizations manage the system through, such as member, application, and entity definition management. Hosted in-process by the platform only.",[274,387,388,393],{},[288,389,390],{},[225,391,392],{},"system",[288,394,395],{},"Platform-internal services. Only system participants can call or host them.",[210,397,398,399,402,403,405],{},"Organization and application ids become zone labels, but only ever after the ",[225,400,401],{},"app"," prefix, so they cannot collide with the platform's own zones. The one exception is guarded explicitly: creating an organization or application whose name slugifies to ",[225,404,392],{}," is rejected.",[210,407,408,409,411,412,415,416,418],{},"Which zones a connection may address is determined by the authenticated participant. A participant may also address any sub-zone of a zone it is allowed, so ",[225,410,365],{}," is reachable by whoever may reach ",[225,413,414],{},"app.acme-org.orders-app",". An address without a ",[225,417,339],{}," carries no zone at all and is only reachable by system participants.",[268,420,421,434],{},[271,422,423],{},[274,424,425,428,431],{},[277,426,427],{},"Participant",[277,429,430],{},"May send to",[277,432,433],{},"May subscribe to",[283,435,436,452,471],{},[274,437,438,441,449],{},[288,439,440],{},"APPLICATION (org, app)",[288,442,443,445,446],{},[225,444,372],{},", ",[225,447,448],{},"app.\u003Corg>.\u003Capp>",[288,450,451],{},"reply destinations only",[274,453,454,457,466],{},[288,455,456],{},"ORGANIZATION (org)",[288,458,459,445,461,445,463],{},[225,460,382],{},[225,462,372],{},[225,464,465],{},"app.\u003Corg>.*",[288,467,468,470],{},[225,469,465],{}," — its applications' zones",[274,472,473,476,479],{},[288,474,475],{},"SYSTEM",[288,477,478],{},"everything",[288,480,481],{},[225,482,392],{},[260,484,486],{"id":485},"resource-name","Resource Name",[210,488,489],{},"The name of the resource being addressed, excluding the zone. For services, this is the fully qualified service name. For streams, this is the event type name.",[218,491,494],{"className":492,"code":493,"language":223},[221],"srv:\u002F\u002Fos-api~com.example.UserService\nstream:\u002F\u002Fapp.acme-org.orders-app~temperature\n",[225,495,493],{"__ignoreMap":227},[260,497,499],{"id":498},"path","Path",[210,501,502],{},"An optional path that identifies a specific part of the resource, such as a method name on a service. The path's case is preserved.",[218,504,507],{"className":505,"code":506,"language":223},[221],"srv:\u002F\u002Fos-api~com.example.UserService\u002FfindById\nstream:\u002F\u002Fapp.acme-org.orders-app~temperature\u002Fsensor-1\n",[225,508,506],{"__ignoreMap":227},[260,510,512],{"id":511},"version","Version",[210,514,515],{},"An optional semantic version for the resource. Enables versioned service routing so multiple versions of a service can coexist.",[218,517,520],{"className":518,"code":519,"language":223},[221],"srv:\u002F\u002Fos-api~com.example.UserService\u002FfindById#1.0.0\nsrv:\u002F\u002Fos-api~com.example.UserService#2.0.0\n",[225,521,519],{"__ignoreMap":227},[206,523,525],{"id":524},"factory-function","Factory Function",[210,527,528,529,5